From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77705: use the Samsung CC state machine and a fixed OTG mode

The mainline charger driver did not follow the Samsung MUIC behaviour:

- It masked most CC and UIC interrupts and never sent the Samsung
  factory-test opcode 0x54 that turns auto VBUS off. Stock leaves the
  masks at UIC 0x04, CC 0x20, PD 0x1c, VDM 0xff and disables auto VBUS.
- It waited for CCStat to become cc_SOURCE before enabling OTG. On this
  MUIC a sink stays at CCStat 0 and only CCPinStat changes, so a USB-C
  flash drive was never seen.
- It derived the boost mode from CNFG_00. The charger block is at 0x00
  here, which selected 0x0a and did not bring VBUS up. 0x0f (buck,
  charger, boost, OTG) is the value that enumerated the drive.

Mirror the stock masks and auto VBUS opcode, trigger OTG on CCPinStat
when VBUS is absent, and latch OTG until the CC pins are released. While
OTG is latched its own boost sets VBUSDET, so VBUSDET must not turn it
off again or the driver toggles forever.

A charger, laptop or other source reports CCStat = SINK. Sink always
wins: it clears the OTG latch and keeps the phone a device, even while
the latch was set. This matters when the phone boots with a laptop
attached, where the CC pins are active before VBUS settles.

A pin-only attach is ambiguous: a source that is being plugged in shows
the same state until its VBUS comes up, at most tCCDebounce (200 ms) plus
tVBUSON (275 ms) later. Stock never sees this, because it waits for
CCStat = cc_SOURCE, which the MUIC firmware debounces itself. Take a
pin-only attach for a sink only after it has held, with the same
CC_STATUS0 and no VBUS, for 500 ms. A CC change restarts the window, and
VBUS, SINK or released pins cancel it. This covers hot-plug, which a
probe-time delay alone never did.

Do not enable OTG for the first three seconds after probe either. With a
source attached at boot VBUSDET can still be clear while it negotiates,
and starting the boost then fights the source and can leave Plasma
Mobile without power. Nothing reports when that has settled, so the hold
stays time-based until the cause is found.

With the CC handling and the probe hold, a SanDisk 3.2Gen1 on the port
enumerated automatically after a hotplug, and a laptop or charger kept the
phone in device mode and charging (verified before the attach debounce
was added).

Serialize the port state: update_port() runs from the USB-C interrupt
thread, from the ordered workqueue and from the probe delay, so it now
takes port_lock, and the probe delay is queued on the ordered workqueue
instead of system_wq. A failed CC or PD status read leaves the state
alone instead of reading as a detach, which dropped a live OTG session.
If enabling OTG fails (current limit, mode or role switch), undo it and
drop the request so the port goes back to sink handling.

Take the role switch before the work items exist and put it through its
own devm action, so it outlives the interrupts and the OTG work and is
not leaked when probe fails later. On removal, forbid new OTG requests
and flush the OTG work before switching the boost off.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c | 294 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 include/linux/power/max77705_charger.h  |   9 +
 2 files changed, 257 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
index 2fdf027cd..b1ff54d3b 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
@@ -29,6 +29,24 @@ static const char *max77705_charger_manufacturer	= "Maxim Integrated";
 static int max77705_charger_set_otg(struct max77705_charger_data *chg, bool enable);
 static void max77705_otg_work(struct work_struct *work);
 
+/*
+ * How long a pin-only attach (CCPinStat set, CCStat still no connection,
+ * no VBUS) must hold before it is taken for a sink to power. A source
+ * that is being plugged in shows the same state first: it debounces its
+ * CC termination for tCCDebounce (100-200 ms) and then has tVBUSON (at
+ * most 275 ms) to drive VBUS (USB Type-C Specification, Release 2.x,
+ * section 4.11). 200 + 275 ms is the latest its VBUS can appear; 500 ms
+ * covers that with margin and is still well below what a user notices
+ * when plugging in a flash drive.
+ *
+ * Stock never needs this: it starts the boost on CCStat = cc_SOURCE
+ * (max77705_cc.c, max77705_vbus_turn_on_ctrl()), which the MAX77705
+ * firmware reports only after its own CC debounce. On this unit a sink
+ * never reaches cc_SOURCE, so the driver has to act on the undebounced
+ * CCPinStat and do the debounce itself.
+ */
+#define MAX77705_OTG_ATTACH_DEBOUNCE_MS	500
+
 static const struct regmap_config max77705_chg_regmap_config = {
 	.reg_base = MAX77705_CHG_REG_BASE,
 	.reg_bits = 8,
@@ -122,15 +140,34 @@ static int max77705_charger_enable(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
 	return rv;
 }
 
+static void max77705_charger_put_role_sw(void *data)
+{
+	struct max77705_charger_data *chg = data;
+
+	usb_role_switch_put(chg->role_sw);
+}
+
 static void max77705_charger_disable(void *data)
 {
 	struct max77705_charger_data *chg = data;
 	int rv;
 
+	/*
+	 * The USB-C interrupt is still live here (devm frees it after this
+	 * action). Forbid new OTG requests first, then flush the OTG work,
+	 * so nothing turns the boost back on after it is switched off.
+	 */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&chg->otg_delay_work);
+	mutex_lock(&chg->port_lock);
+	chg->otg_allowed = false;
+	chg->otg_requested = false;
+	mutex_unlock(&chg->port_lock);
+	/* otg_allowed is false, so update_port() cannot re-arm it any more */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&chg->otg_attach_work);
+	cancel_work_sync(&chg->otg_work);
+
 	if (chg->otg_on)
 		max77705_charger_set_otg(chg, false);
-	if (chg->role_sw)
-		usb_role_switch_put(chg->role_sw);
 
 	rv = regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_CHG_EN], MAX77705_CHG_DISABLE);
 	if (rv)
@@ -700,44 +737,100 @@ static int max77705_charger_apply_port_current(struct max77705_charger_data *chg
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static int max77705_charger_update_port(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
+/*
+ * Called from the USB-C interrupt thread and from the ordered workqueue, so
+ * the port state and the OTG request are serialized by port_lock. Nothing
+ * in here may issue a USB-C opcode: the opcode reply arrives through the
+ * same interrupt thread, which could be waiting for this lock.
+ */
+static int __max77705_charger_update_port(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
 {
 	unsigned int port, status;
-	unsigned int cc_status0 = 0, pd_status1 = 0;
-	u8 cc_stat;
-	bool data_role_host;
+	unsigned int cc_status0, pd_status1;
+	u8 cc_stat, cc_pin;
 	int ret;
 
+	lockdep_assert_held(&chg->port_lock);
+
 	ret = regmap_read(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_BC_STATUS, &status);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A failed read must not look like a detach: that would drop a live
+	 * OTG session. Keep the current state and wait for the next event.
+	 */
 	ret = regmap_read(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_CC_STATUS0, &cc_status0);
 	if (ret)
-		cc_status0 = 0;
+		return ret;
 
 	ret = regmap_read(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_PD_STATUS1, &pd_status1);
 	if (ret)
-		pd_status1 = 0;
+		return ret;
 
 	cc_stat = cc_status0 & MAX77705_USBC_CC_STATUS0_CCSTAT;
-	data_role_host = !!(pd_status1 & MAX77705_USBC_PD_STATUS1_DATAROLE);
+	cc_pin = (cc_status0 & MAX77705_USBC_CC_STATUS0_CCPINSTAT) >>
+		 __ffs(MAX77705_USBC_CC_STATUS0_CCPINSTAT);
 
 	dev_dbg(chg->dev, "update_port: BC 0x%02x CC0 0x%02x PD1 0x%02x\n",
 		status, cc_status0, pd_status1);
 
-	if (cc_stat == MAX77705_CC_SOURCE || (data_role_host && !(status & MAX77705_USBC_BC_STATUS_VBUSDET))) {
-		if (!chg->otg_requested) {
-			chg->otg_requested = true;
+	/*
+	 * A charger, laptop or other source reports CCStat = SINK. The phone
+	 * must stay a sink/device in that case, even if OTG was latched
+	 * before the source was detected. Only a source role or an open CC
+	 * pin pair with no VBUS starts OTG.
+	 */
+	if (cc_stat == MAX77705_CC_SINK) {
+		if (chg->otg_requested) {
+			chg->otg_requested = false;
 			queue_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->otg_work);
 		}
-	} else if (cc_stat == MAX77705_CC_NO_CONN || (status & MAX77705_USBC_BC_STATUS_VBUSDET)) {
-		if (chg->otg_requested) {
+	} else if (chg->otg_on || chg->otg_requested) {
+		/*
+		 * Our own OTG boost sets VBUSDET. Ignore VBUS while latched and
+		 * release only when the CC pins are gone.
+		 */
+		if (!cc_pin && cc_stat == MAX77705_CC_NO_CONN) {
 			chg->otg_requested = false;
 			queue_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->otg_work);
 		}
+	} else if (chg->otg_allowed && cc_stat == MAX77705_CC_SOURCE) {
+		/* the MUIC's own debounced verdict: power the sink now */
+		chg->otg_requested = true;
+		queue_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->otg_work);
+	} else if (chg->otg_allowed && cc_stat == MAX77705_CC_NO_CONN && cc_pin &&
+		   !(status & MAX77705_USBC_BC_STATUS_VBUSDET)) {
+		/*
+		 * A pin-only attach: a sink, or a source whose VBUS is not up
+		 * yet. Take it for a sink only once it has held for the whole
+		 * debounce. A change of CC_STATUS0 within it (the other pin, a
+		 * CCIStat step) restarts the window, also when it is only seen
+		 * at the end of the window (not every CC bit interrupts); an
+		 * interrupt that leaves the state as it was does not; anything
+		 * that is no longer a pin-only attach cancels it below.
+		 */
+		if (chg->otg_attach_settled && cc_status0 == chg->otg_attach_cc0) {
+			chg->otg_requested = true;
+			queue_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->otg_work);
+		} else if (!delayed_work_pending(&chg->otg_attach_work) ||
+			   cc_status0 != chg->otg_attach_cc0) {
+			chg->otg_attach_cc0 = cc_status0;
+			mod_delayed_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->otg_attach_work,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(MAX77705_OTG_ATTACH_DEBOUNCE_MS));
+		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * VBUS came up, the source resolved to SINK, the pins went away or
+	 * OTG is already on: no attach is waiting for its debounce. A run
+	 * that is already waiting for port_lock re-reads the state and does
+	 * nothing.
+	 */
+	if (chg->otg_on || chg->otg_requested || cc_stat != MAX77705_CC_NO_CONN ||
+	    !cc_pin || (status & MAX77705_USBC_BC_STATUS_VBUSDET))
+		cancel_delayed_work(&chg->otg_attach_work);
+
 	if (chg->otg_on || chg->otg_requested)
 		return 0;
 
@@ -781,6 +874,17 @@ static int max77705_charger_update_port(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int max77705_charger_update_port(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	mutex_lock(&chg->port_lock);
+	ret = __max77705_charger_update_port(chg);
+	mutex_unlock(&chg->port_lock);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /*
  * The USB-C block's opcode mailbox (Samsung max77705_i2c_opcode_write/read):
  * the opcode and its data go to 0x21, 0x41 ends a short command, the block
@@ -843,7 +947,69 @@ static void max77705_otg_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct max77705_charger_data *chg =
 		container_of(work, struct max77705_charger_data, otg_work);
 
-	max77705_charger_set_otg(chg, chg->otg_requested);
+	bool enable;
+	int ret;
+
+	mutex_lock(&chg->port_lock);
+	enable = chg->otg_requested;
+	mutex_unlock(&chg->port_lock);
+
+	/* not under port_lock: set_otg() waits for a USB-C opcode reply */
+	ret = max77705_charger_set_otg(chg, enable);
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * Drop the request so update_port() applies the sink state
+		 * again; the next CC interrupt asks for OTG once more. Do not
+		 * call update_port() from here, or a persistent failure would
+		 * retry in a loop.
+		 */
+		dev_err(chg->dev, "failed to %s OTG: %d\n",
+			enable ? "enable" : "disable", ret);
+		mutex_lock(&chg->port_lock);
+		chg->otg_requested = chg->otg_on;
+		mutex_unlock(&chg->port_lock);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* apply the sink currents again once OTG has released the port */
+	if (!chg->otg_on)
+		max77705_charger_update_port(chg);
+}
+
+static void max77705_otg_delay_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct max77705_charger_data *chg =
+		container_of(work, struct max77705_charger_data,
+			     otg_delay_work.work);
+
+	/*
+	 * Do not start OTG during the first seconds of probe. With a charger
+	 * plugged at boot, VBUSDET can be clear while the charger negotiates
+	 * (for how long was never measured), and enabling the boost then
+	 * fought the charger and left the phone without power. Neither this
+	 * driver nor stock reports an event for "the boot-time CC state has
+	 * settled" (stock has no such hold: it waits for cc_SOURCE), so this
+	 * stays the 3 s that was verified on the phone until that cause is
+	 * found. A pin-only attach still goes through the debounce after it.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&chg->port_lock);
+	chg->otg_allowed = true;
+	__max77705_charger_update_port(chg);
+	mutex_unlock(&chg->port_lock);
+}
+
+static void max77705_otg_attach_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct max77705_charger_data *chg =
+		container_of(work, struct max77705_charger_data,
+			     otg_attach_work.work);
+
+	/* re-read the port: OTG starts only if the pin-only attach held */
+	mutex_lock(&chg->port_lock);
+	chg->otg_attach_settled = true;
+	__max77705_charger_update_port(chg);
+	chg->otg_attach_settled = false;
+	mutex_unlock(&chg->port_lock);
 }
 
 static int max77705_charger_set_otg(struct max77705_charger_data *chg, bool enable)
@@ -866,18 +1032,19 @@ static int max77705_charger_set_otg(struct max77705_charger_data *chg, bool enab
 		chg->otg_prev_mode = mode;
 
 		/*
-		 * Stock keeps the buck and charger bits that are already on and
-		 * adds boost and OTG: 0x5 (buck and charger) becomes 0xF, 0x4
-		 * (buck only) becomes 0xE, and an all-off charger becomes 0xA.
-		 * Writing 0xA on top of a charger mode leaves the buck path off
-		 * and the boost does not come up.
+		 * 0xF is the value the forced OTG test enumerated with:
+		 * buck, charger, boost and OTG all on. Do not derive it from
+		 * the current mode; the charger block can be at 0x00 here.
 		 */
-		if (mode & MAX77705_BUCK_MASK)
-			target = mode | MAX77705_BOOST_MASK | MAX77705_OTG_MASK;
-		else
-			target = MAX77705_BOOST_MASK | MAX77705_OTG_MASK;
+		target = MAX77705_CHG_MASK | MAX77705_BUCK_MASK |
+			 MAX77705_BOOST_MASK | MAX77705_OTG_MASK;
 
-		regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_OTG_ILIM], MAX77705_OTG_ILIM_1500);
+		ret = regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_OTG_ILIM],
+					 MAX77705_OTG_ILIM_1500);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(chg->dev, "failed to set the OTG current limit: %d\n", ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
 
 		/*
 		 * This runs from the ordered workqueue, not from the threaded
@@ -896,8 +1063,15 @@ static int max77705_charger_set_otg(struct max77705_charger_data *chg, bool enab
 			return ret;
 		}
 
-		if (chg->role_sw)
-			usb_role_switch_set_role(chg->role_sw, USB_ROLE_HOST);
+		if (chg->role_sw) {
+			ret = usb_role_switch_set_role(chg->role_sw, USB_ROLE_HOST);
+			if (ret) {
+				dev_err(chg->dev, "failed to switch to host: %d\n", ret);
+				regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_MODE],
+						   chg->otg_prev_mode);
+				return ret;
+			}
+		}
 
 		chg->otg_on = true;
 	} else {
@@ -1177,26 +1351,32 @@ static int max77705_charger_setup_usbc(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = regmap_update_bits(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_UIC_INT_M,
-				 MAX77705_USBC_UIC_INT_APCMDRES |
-				 MAX77705_USBC_UIC_INT_VBUSDET |
-				 MAX77705_USBC_UIC_INT_CHGTYP, 0);
+	ret = regmap_write(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_UIC_INT_M, 0x04);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_write(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_CC_INT_M, 0x20);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = regmap_update_bits(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_CC_INT_M,
-				 MAX77705_USBC_CC_INT_CCSTAT |
-				 MAX77705_USBC_CC_INT_CCISTAT |
-				 MAX77705_USBC_CC_INT_CCPINSTAT, 0);
+	ret = regmap_write(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_PD_INT_M, 0x1c);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = regmap_update_bits(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_PD_INT_M,
-				 MAX77705_USBC_PD_INT_DATAROLE |
-				 (chg->pd_max_power_mw ? MAX77705_USBC_PD_INT_PSRDY : 0), 0);
+	ret = regmap_write(chg->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_REG_VDM_INT_M, 0xff);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* stock max77705_init_opcode(): turn off the auto VBUS test mode */
+	{
+		u8 auto_vbus = 0;
+
+		ret = max77705_usbc_cmd(chg, MAX77705_OP_SAMSUNG_FACTORY_TEST,
+					&auto_vbus, 1, NULL, 0);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(chg->dev, "failed to disable auto VBUS: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
 	/* stock max77705_set_snkcap(): the sink caps it offers to sources */
 	if (chg->snkcap_len)
 		max77705_usbc_cmd(chg, MAX77705_OP_SET_SNKCAP, chg->snkcap,
@@ -1211,6 +1391,8 @@ static int max77705_charger_setup_usbc(struct max77705_charger_data *chg)
 	if (chg->pd_max_power_mw)
 		queue_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->pd_work);
 
+	queue_delayed_work(chg->wqueue, &chg->otg_delay_work, msecs_to_jiffies(3000));
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1459,6 +1641,26 @@ static int max77705_charger_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	if (!chg->wqueue)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	ret = devm_mutex_init(dev, &chg->port_lock);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Get the role switch before the work items are set up, so devm puts
+	 * it only after the interrupts are freed and the works are cancelled.
+	 */
+	chg->role_sw = usb_role_switch_get(dev);
+	if (IS_ERR(chg->role_sw)) {
+		if (PTR_ERR(chg->role_sw) == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		dev_warn(dev, "usb-role-switch not found: %ld\n", PTR_ERR(chg->role_sw));
+		chg->role_sw = NULL;
+	} else if (chg->role_sw) {
+		ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, max77705_charger_put_role_sw, chg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	ret = devm_work_autocancel(dev, &chg->chgin_work, max77705_chgin_isr_work);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize interrupt work\n");
@@ -1469,6 +1671,14 @@ static int max77705_charger_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 	ret = devm_work_autocancel(dev, &chg->otg_work, max77705_otg_work);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &chg->otg_delay_work,
+					   max77705_otg_delay_work);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &chg->otg_attach_work,
+					   max77705_otg_attach_work);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 	ret = devm_delayed_work_autocancel(dev, &chg->afc_work, max77705_afc_work);
@@ -1479,14 +1689,6 @@ static int max77705_charger_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize charger IC\n");
 
-	chg->role_sw = usb_role_switch_get(dev);
-	if (IS_ERR(chg->role_sw)) {
-		if (PTR_ERR(chg->role_sw) == -EPROBE_DEFER)
-			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
-		dev_warn(dev, "usb-role-switch not found: %ld\n", PTR_ERR(chg->role_sw));
-		chg->role_sw = NULL;
-	}
-
 	ret = max77705_charger_setup_usbc(chg);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to set up cable detection\n");
diff --git a/include/linux/power/max77705_charger.h b/include/linux/power/max77705_charger.h
index 8dabb5e6b..4c7d6e600 100644
--- a/include/linux/power/max77705_charger.h
+++ b/include/linux/power/max77705_charger.h
@@ -151,11 +151,13 @@
 #define MAX77705_USBC_REG_UIC_INT_M	0x0e
 #define MAX77705_USBC_REG_CC_INT_M	0x0f
 #define MAX77705_USBC_REG_PD_INT_M	0x10
+#define MAX77705_USBC_REG_VDM_INT_M	0x11
 
 #define MAX77705_USBC_CC_INT_CCSTAT	BIT(0)
 #define MAX77705_USBC_CC_INT_CCISTAT	BIT(2)
 #define MAX77705_USBC_CC_INT_CCPINSTAT	BIT(3)
 #define MAX77705_USBC_CC_STATUS0_CCSTAT	GENMASK(2, 0)
+#define MAX77705_USBC_CC_STATUS0_CCPINSTAT	GENMASK(7, 6)
